ce-paper-text-army-orders = [bold]Order of the Commander-in-Chief of the Imperial Army to the settlement garrison.[/bold]

    Due to the growing threat to the population and assets of the Empire, the city guard has been reinforced by a permanent garrison of His Majesty's Imperial Army. We hereby send instructions for the garrison's work:

    1. The army is not the guard. Do not take on the duty of keeping order in the settlement, and do not investigate anything except significant threats to the settlement.

    2. A significant threat is anyone who poses an imminent danger to the lives of the citizens.

    3. The army cannot and must not protect the property of private persons. The army's resources and personnel may not be used for personal purposes or for profit.

    4. The army must respond to significant security threats, but in the absence of such threats the garrison may be dismissed by the Commandant.

    5. Only the Commandant has the right to dispose of the army's resources and personnel. A soldier acting against the Commandant's orders must be dismissed from service. The Commandant has the right to hire temporary personnel if circumstances require it.
